knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3688
What it fixes: A module that starts with a hashbang line (`#!/usr/bin/env node`) and also contains CommonJS
syntax goes through vite-plugin-commonjs, which prepends a `module`/`exports` facade and so pushes
`#!` off byte 0, the only place it is valid; the bundler's parser then rejects the build.
This is the maintainer's version: the displaced hashbang is turned into a `//` line comment (same
length, so source maps hold) both in vinext's CommonJS transform wrapper and in the client dependency
optimizer (new dist/plugins/commonjs-hashbang.js). The upstream ESM-facade check it also precedes is
not in 1.0.1, so it is not ported.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3688.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

